/-!
# Inner-family branch of odd-prime PSU₃ generation

`Reduction` constructs a common Sylow-central socle involution in every
nontrivial inner family member. It also proves the E₀, Sylow, radical-rank
and solvable-quotient steps that turn component structure on the centralizer
residual supplement into containment of the full centralizer.

The local component structure (with the solvable p = 3 alternative) and the
remaining unitary generation geometry are still required. This module does
not yet export the unconditional inner-family exclusion of E.1.14(7).

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, E.1.14(7), printed p.214, and A.3.21, printed p.55;
Aschbacher, *GF(2)-representations of finite groups* (1982), Lemma 4.11.
-/
